#16713
Deep in the Lake~
   The fresh water is cool and clear.  You can see all of the lake bed, stretch
out almost a league in every direction.  What little light that penetrates the
rippling surface, far above, poorly illuminates this part of the lake.  The
lake bed's center is twenty yards below you and curves upwards in all
directions.  There are some small caves and fauna growing out of the bed south
of here.  To the east lies a couple shallow caves.  A warm water fissure spews
forth to the north.    
~
